 JUNICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATO MASARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMODAIRA KENICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAYASHI, JUNICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, MASARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMODAIRA, KENICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of forming an undercut in a metal powder injection-molded article and a metal powder injection-molded article having an undercut formed by such method. The method comprises the steps of injection-molding a mixture that contains metal powder and binding resin, forming an undercut in an injection-molded article obtained by the injection molding, and degreasing and sintering the injection-molded article formed with the undercut. It is preferable that the undercut be formed by deforming at least a part of the injection-molded article and more preferable that it be deformed by pressing using a pressing member.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un procédé de formation d'une saignée dans un article moulé par injection d'une poudre métallique et sur l'article ainsi formé. Ledit procédé consiste à mouler par injection un mélange de poudre métallique et de résine, à pratiquer une saignée dans l'article ainsi obtenu, puis à le dégraisser et le fritter. La saignée se fera de préférence en déformant au moins une partie de l'article, et de préférence par pressage à la presse.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>